# /sdd-backup

Purpose:
  Create timestamped backups of critical .sdd/ files with automatic rotation of old backups.

Owns: commands\sdd-backup.sdd
Description:
  Create timestamped backup of critical .sdd/ files. Old backups are
  rotated automatically.

Usage:
  /sdd-backup
  /sdd-backup --name=<name>
  /sdd-backup --list

Options:
  --name  Custom backup name (default: timestamp)
  --list  List existing backups

Backup:
  Location: .runtime/backup/
  Files: PROJECT.sdd, INDEX.sdd, chains/, decisions/, project/
  Manifest: timestamp, file hashes, system version
  Rotation: keep last 10

Exit Codes:
  0 - Success
  1 - Failed
  2 - No files found

Navigation:
  INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
  RestoreCommand: @sdd-restore.sdd
  Timeline: @../timeline/INDEX.sdd

State: +
